/* kit/boxes.css: the app's kit/boxes.css as forked with tunerloop-dash. Yours to change. */
/* The kit's boxes: the type scale, a panel as a size container, and each box's own styles (the dial,
   the big number, the Lambda Twin, the phone boxes, the grid of numbers, the charts). Colours and
   fonts: themes.css. */
/* The type scale: five sizes every box uses, from the panel's size. kit.js typeScale() gives the canvas
   views the same steps, and the Screens page's Type & colour panel shows them all.
     lbl   labels, units beside small numbers, axis text (caps, 600, letter-spaced)
     small grid values, the unit beside a hero number, rates
     value secondary numbers (Pull cells, G now, stats)
     big   two numbers stacked (the Lambda Twin)
     hero  the one main number (big boxes, Speed, Pull RPM, Oil)
   Numbers are 700 and tabular; the dial draws its own text in dial units, so it scales with the dial.
   The rule: big is the least for any number meant to be read at a glance while driving; value
   and small are for detail read parked (full screen history, labels). */
